// Package elanrt is the runtime of the programs generated by elanc-go
// (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-s7-go-compiler-design.md,
// decisions G2-G4).
//
// The pieces, one file each:
//
//   - term.go, table.go, strings.go: terms. One node type ([Node]) for
//     every sort, maximally shared through a weak unique table: two equal
//     terms alive at the same time are the same pointer.
//   - ac.go: AC multisets, ordered by a history-independent structural
//     order ([Compare]), and the helpers of AC matching.
//   - strat.go: strategies in continuation-passing style ([K], [Strat]).
//   - builtin.go: int (32-bit wrap), bool and string builtins with the
//     interpreter's semantics; stuck terms of builtin sorts.
//   - print.go: the printer of the compiled C programs ([Writer]).
//   - driver.go: options, output, statistics, [Main].
//   - depth.go: the recursion guard ([Guard]), exit status 3.
//
// A program works on its terms from one goroutine (the one started by
// [Main]): the runtime has no locks on its hot paths. Standard library
// only, no unsafe.
package elanrt
